  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Friday)\nIssued at 1024 PM CDT Thu Jul 23 2026\n\nThe start of the new week will bring more heat. Strong high \npressure sets up over the central US, and temperatures across \nMiddle TN will be on the rise. On Sunday, highs warm back up into\nthe low-90s west of the Plateau and will continue to trend up \ninto the mid and upper-90s through the first half of the week. \nTuesday will be the hottest day of the week with afternoon \ntemperatures getting close to triple digits. Heat index values \nwill certainly be in the triple digits, resulting in major heat \nrisk. So be sure to stay hydrated and take frequent breaks if \nyou're outdoors a lot. As far as rain goes, only low rain chances \n(10-30%) are in the forecast each afternoon through next week. The\nheat looks to break by Wednesday or Thursday with the arrival of \na front.",
